; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Peano Curve
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Advanced
; TAGS:     recursion, space filling curve, mutual recursion, L-system
; SUMMARY:  Draws Peano's 1890 space filling curve with two procedures that call each other.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Giuseppe Peano found the first curve that passes through every
;   point of a square. This program draws the turtle version: a
;   single path that zigzags through a 81 by 81 grid, built from nine
;   smaller copies of itself, each a mirror image of its neighbors.
;   The color fades from teal to purple along the path.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the level on the last line (1 to 4). Level 5
;   has 59049 steps and is slow.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * mutual recursion: PEANO.X calls PEANO.Y and the other way round
;   * turning an L-system rule into Logo, symbol by symbol
;   * working out the step length from the level with POWER
;   * coloring by progress with a global counter
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Draw level 1 with a thick pen and trace the S shapes.
;   * Swap LEFT and RIGHT in PEANO.X only. Does it still fill?
;   * Use SETPENSIZE equal to the step to fill the square solid.
; ============================================================

; The L-system for the Peano curve, with angle 90:
;   X -> XFYFX+F+YFXFY-F-XFYFX
;   Y -> YFXFY-F-XFYFX+F+YFXFY
; X and Y are never drawn; they only say where the smaller curves go.
; F is a step, + is a left turn and - is a right turn.

to peano.x :level
  if :level = 0 [stop]
  localmake "n :level - 1
  peano.x :n f peano.y :n f peano.x :n
  left 90 f left 90
  peano.y :n f peano.x :n f peano.y :n
  right 90 f right 90
  peano.x :n f peano.y :n f peano.x :n
end

to peano.y :level
  if :level = 0 [stop]
  localmake "n :level - 1
  peano.y :n f peano.x :n f peano.y :n
  right 90 f right 90
  peano.x :n f peano.y :n f peano.x :n
  left 90 f left 90
  peano.y :n f peano.x :n f peano.y :n
end

; F takes one step, shading the pen by how far along the path we are.
to f
  make "done :done + 1
  localmake "t :done / :steps
  setpencolor (list 40 + 140 * :t 190 - 150 * :t 180 + 40 * :t)
  forward :unit
end

; PEANO sets up the step length so the curve fills a 480 square.
to peano :level
  localmake "cells power 3 :level
  make "unit 480 / (:cells - 1)
  make "steps :cells * :cells - 1
  make "done 0
  ; The curve climbs first and its first turn is a left turn, so it
  ; starts at the bottom right corner and works its way leftward.
  penup setxy 240 -240 setheading 0 pendown
  peano.x :level
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [248 248 244]
setpensize 2
peano 4
